&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring our first dedicated international tax professional in Asia-Pacific, based in Singapore. You&#39;ll be a key member of Anthropic&#39;s tax team, reporting to our Head of International Tax Operations / Business Advisory and working closely with tax colleagues in Dublin and our San Francisco headquarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As APAC Tax Lead, you&#39;ll own direct tax compliance and advisory across our Asia-Pacific entities and operations (Japan, Korea, India, Singapore, Australia, Taiwan) and help build tax infrastructure to support Anthropic&#39;s rapid international expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead APAC direct tax compliance, working with external advisors (KPMG, PwC, Deloitte) to ensure timely and accurate filings across all jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support transfer pricing documentation and intercompany transactions for APAC entities, including cost-plus arrangements and intercompany service agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage withholding tax positions and treaty relief on cross-border flows, including customer receipts and vendor payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on permanent establishment risks, entity structuring, and operational tax considerations as Anthropic expands APAC commercial and infrastructure activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the tax side of regional infrastructure expansion, including data center, colocation, and subsea cable arrangements and new entity formations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with indirect tax personnel on VAT/GST and consumption tax matters to align on tax strategy and overall compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Legal, and People teams on payroll taxes, equity compensation, and employee mobility matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with local tax authorities and manage any inquiries or audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to global tax projects including public company readiness, SOX compliance, and tax technology implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with indirect tax team on advisory and compliance and audit assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of corporate tax in one or more major APAC jurisdictions and cross-border tax issues across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with transfer pricing documentation, intercompany agreements, and withholding tax and treaty analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA, CA, CTA, or equivalent professional qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to work across time zones with US and European colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who thrives in ambiguity and can build processes from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of international tax experience, ideally with a mix of Big 4/advisory and in-house roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to technology or high-growth company tax matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the tax aspects of data center or infrastructure buildouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Pillar Two/global minimum tax rules and digital services taxes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Indian direct tax matters, including permanent establishment and withholding tax issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting IPO readiness or public company tax compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with systems buildout or automation&lt;/li&gt;
