&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s customer-facing teams are often the first place a customer sees what Claude can do. As a Demo Engineer, you&#39;ll build the demos, reference implementations, and reusable tooling that help those teams make new capabilities tangible, relevant, and trustworthy, ideally within days of a product launch rather than weeks after.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits between product engineering, technical storytelling, and GTM execution. You&#39;ll own ambiguous, high-leverage problems end to end: prototyping an agentic experience for a new capability, then hardening it into something reliable that other teams can run on their own. You&#39;ll work closely with Product, Engineering, Marketing, Operations, and our sales and solutions teams, and you&#39;ll bring what you learn from customer-facing work back to the people building the products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because a demo is frequently someone&#39;s first impression of what our models can and can&#39;t do, accuracy and honesty matter as much as polish. Success in this role looks like customer-facing teams demonstrating new capabilities sooner and with more confidence, recurring requests becoming reusable assets rather than one-off projects, and field insights shaping product and launch-readiness decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own demo readiness for new and priority Claude capabilities, including environments, integrations, synthetic data, evaluations, reliability checks, and fallback paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes, agents, and reference flows that make complex capabilities concrete and tie them to clear customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring requests into reusable accelerators such as companion apps, templates, Skills, plugins, and self-service demo packages that scale across customer-facing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM colleagues on high-impact customer moments, unblock critical technical gaps, and spot the patterns worth turning into shared assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal agentic systems that automate demo preparation, validation, and asset maintenance, so demos stay current as products change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate patterns from customer-facing work into product feedback, launch-readiness priorities, and systemic improvements with Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and raise the bar for demo quality across accuracy, safety, reliability, usability, and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide when a customer need calls for a bespoke build and when it should become a shared capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python or TypeScript, with experience shipping working software end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building applications or agents on top of LLM APIs, including prompting, tool use, and retrieval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing integrations with third-party APIs, data sources, and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to take an ambiguous capability or customer need to a working prototype quickly, and then make it reliable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication of technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences, including sales and solutions teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort collaborating across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Operations, and GTM teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a demo engineering, solutions engineering, sales engineering, forward deployed engineering, developer relations, or product engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building reusable internal tools, templates, or self-service assets that other teams adopted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Claude Code, the Claude Agent SDK, the Model Context Protocol (MCP), Skills, or plugins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building evaluation or validation harnesses for AI systems, including reliability checks and graceful fallbacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building always-on or scheduled agentic systems that automate internal workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building synthetic or sanitized datasets that make demos realistic without exposing sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Front-end or product design skills that help demos feel polished and intuitive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting product launches or running launch-readiness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of turning field feedback into concrete product input that influenced a roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for making powerful technology safe and beneficial, and a commitment to representing model capabilities accurately and honestly&lt;/li&gt;
