&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-lfile-container=&quot;8ef30c43-ab32-4541-a717-ad7fc0db1513&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Discovery team at Anthropic is organized around the north star goal of building an AI scientist – a system capable of solving the long-term reasoning challenges and basic capabilities necessary to push the scientific and technological frontier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re expanding our work on engineering and the applied sciences. Our goal is to contribute to training Claude to invent, design, and engineer across every discipline and scale, reliably and safely: new manufacturing and experimental techniques, processes, materials, devices, instruments, machines, energy systems, and factories. We want this work to accelerate science and technology and benefit people widely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking exceptional researchers with deep expertise in one or more of these areas. In this role, you&#39;ll work at the intersection of frontier AI and your field, developing rigorous methods to measure and improve Claude&#39;s performance on complex engineering and scientific tasks. You&#39;ll collaborate closely with researchers, engineers, and partners across Anthropic and industry to build AI systems that can engage in all phases of research and development, and to test Claude&#39;s designs against real-world feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement evaluation methodologies for assessing AI model capabilities relevant to engineering and applied science research and applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design realistic tasks and training environments, and curate data from your field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and validate simulations and computational tools for your field, and calibrate them against real-world data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with industry partners, manufacturers, and labs to build and test what Claude invents, designs, and engineers, and bring that real-world feedback into evaluation and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think through how Claude&#39;s engineering capabilities can permeate the real world: where they can have the most impact across industry and research, and what it takes to get them adopted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise the team on which problems, tools, and workflows matter most in your field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with domain experts and partners to establish benchmarks and gather high-quality data for training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate between engineering domain knowledge and machine learning objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise and hands-on R&amp;amp;D or industry experience in an engineering or applied science discipline, such as mechanical, electrical, materials, chemical, aerospace, structural, industrial, or manufacturing engineering; applied physics; computational simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI or machine learning, whether evaluating and training AI systems or applying these tools in your field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of taking work from concept through to a working result, such as a product, process, device, experiment, or tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on proficiency with the computational design, analysis, or simulation tools used in your field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic programming proficiency, for example in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity and develop solutions in a rapidly evolving research environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating closely with cross-functional teams, and to explain your field clearly to people outside it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to using AI to accelerate engineering and scientific progress while maintaining high ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on R&amp;amp;D or industry experience in an engineering or applied science discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ph.D. in an engineering or applied science field, or equivalent industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in product design and manufacturing, or in developing engineering or scientific simulation software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breadth across more than one discipline, or across several stages of the path from design to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern AI model training methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building high-fidelity solvers or simulation engines that were validated against real-world data and used in practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with manufacturers, vendors, contract research organizations, or academic labs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing data pipelines and working with large-scale technical datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications, patents, or contributions to open-source scientific or engineering software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$320,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$405,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run the external audit calendar for our SOX 404 program as we scale toward an IPO. That means coordinating with our external auditors across the year, aligning testing windows with control owners, educating our control owners, and keeping requests and deliverables on schedule. You will also own SOX scoping and risk assessment cycles, deficiency tracking, and status reporting, and help roll out our GRC platform so the program runs from one system of record instead of spreadsheets. You will scale the program through AI-enabled workflows that reduce manual effort and speed up our SOX program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Head of Business Controls and works closely with everyone on the SOX and Internal Audit team. This is an individual contributor role for someone who keeps a complex program on schedule, writes clearly, and makes the program simpler each cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual SOX audit calendar, including interim and year-end testing windows, walkthrough schedules, and key deliverable dates agreed with external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the day-to-day point of contact for external auditor requests. Triage, route, and track each request to closure, including PBC (provided-by-client) lists and evidence deliveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate auditor walkthroughs and fieldwork with process owners, control owners, and the SOX Testing team, so each control owner is asked for the same evidence once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track auditor findings, management responses, and deficiency follow-ups, and report status to Internal Audit leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare control owners and process owners for auditor sessions, and get evidence delivered on time without direct authority over them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the annual SOX scoping and risk assessment, including quarterly refreshes, and support the annual Fraud Risk Assessment, so the program has appropriate scope and coverage under COSO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor BP and IT SOX testing and report status to leadership and share status with external auditors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead work with the business to improve control documentation, including education of templates and SOX guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find optimization and automation opportunities across the SOX lifecycle through the use of AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the rollout of the GRC tool for SOX, including control libraries, workflows, evidence requests, and testing templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the data and reporting requirements the platform must meet, and test that it produces what the program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the quarterly sub-certification process and report results to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own SOX program status reporting: dashboards and metrics for leadership, audit calendar progress, and deficiency and remediation status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own status reporting for the full SOX lifecycle: scoping and risk assessment, testing, deficiencies and remediation, segregation of duties (SOD), SOC 1 report reviews, the fraud risk assessment, and audit calendar progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big 4 audit firm experience on SOX 404 or ICFR engagements, including managing audit calendars, PBC requests, and fieldwork with external audit teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with external auditor teams on requests, testing schedules, and findings, from the company side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of hands-on SOX 404 experience, including scoping, risk assessment, control documentation, testing, and deficiency evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the COSO framework, ICFR, and PCAOB standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or maintaining Risk and Control Matrices and process documentation or flowcharts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing or administering a GRC systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reporting program status, metrics, and issues to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to get control owners to deliver on time without authority over them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear writing and calm coordination under deadline pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in a related field or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house SOX experience at a pre-IPO or newly public company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a fraud risk assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA, CISA, or similar certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL or data tools for reporting, and experience building lightweight automations, including with Claude.&lt;/li&gt;
