&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in GTM, revenue or finance systems roles&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with usage-based or consumption pricing, and with billing platforms such as Stripe, Metronome or Zuora&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience moving existing customers onto new pricing, including migrations, grandfathering and amendments at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with tax setup for new products (tax codes, tax engines such as Anrok or Avalara)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with integrations between Salesforce and billing, ERP or provisioning systems, and comfort reading API payloads and integration logs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Basic SQL and comfort using a data warehouse to check launch data&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce Administrator certification. CPQ Specialist, Advanced Administrator or Business Analyst certification is a plus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on use of AI tools (Claude or similar) in how you design, build or document systems, and the ability to explain how you check their output&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
