&lt;p&gt;As a Field Executive Architect, you will serve as Anthropic&#39;s senior technical voice with our most strategic customers. You&#39;ll engage directly with C-suite executives and senior technical leaders at the world&#39;s largest enterprises to understand their business, align stakeholders around a clear vision for how AI fits into their strategy, and create momentum toward adoption of Anthropic&#39;s products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a hands-on-keyboard engineering role. Your job is to walk into a room full of executives, quickly understand their business and technical landscape, and help them see a clear path forward with Claude. You&#39;ll then partner with Sales and Applied AI teams to ensure that vision translates into execution -- checking in on high-momentum accounts, maintaining executive relationships, and keeping deals on track. Internally, you&#39;ll serve as a sponsor for enterprise customer needs, working with Product to ensure that what matters most to our largest accounts is heard and prioritized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll bring deep experience in enterprise technology and a track record of operating at the intersection of business strategy and technical execution. Whether you&#39;ve been a CTO, VP of Engineering, Field CTO, or a world-class senior technical salesperson, what matters is that you&#39;ve seen how large organizations make technology decisions and can meet executives where they are -- with credibility, clarity, and conviction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engage directly with C-suite and senior technical leaders at Anthropic&#39;s largest and most strategic accounts, aligning business and technical stakeholders around a clear vision for AI adoption&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare for and lead high-stakes customer engagements -- executive briefings, EBCs, on-site workshops -- that change the trajectory of key accounts at critical inflection points&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Sales and Applied AI teams before and after engagements to game plan approach, debrief on outcomes, and ensure the vision carries through to execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lean in on high-momentum accounts after initial engagement, maintaining executive relationships, providing strategic guidance to the Sales and Applied AI teams, and sustaining deal momentum&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as an internal sponsor for enterprise customer needs, translating field feedback into clear priorities for Product and ensuring the most important enterprise requirements are heard and acted on&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge the gap between our field organization and Product org -- helping each side understand the other&#39;s priorities, constraints, and roadmap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel regularly to customer sites for executive engagements, workshops, and strategic account meetings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15+ years of experience in enterprise technology, with significant time spent in senior technical leadership or senior technical sales roles (CTO, VP of Engineering, Chief Architect, Field CTO, or similar)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of engaging credibly with C-suite executives and senior technical leaders at large enterprises -- you can hold the room and earn trust quickly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep understanding of how large organizations evaluate, buy, and scale technology -- you&#39;ve seen the inside of these decisions from a leadership seat or from the sales side of the table&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enough technical depth to understand modern AI systems and their enterprise applications, and enough business acumen to connect technical capabilities to business outcomes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience translating between technical and business audiences -- you can make complex topics clear and compelling for both&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong opinions about what makes enterprise technology adoption succeed or fail, informed by having led or closely advised these efforts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ability to navigate ambiguity and move fast in a rapidly evolving market -- you&#39;re comfortable operating without a detailed playbook and building the plane while flying it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A collaborative mindset -- sales at Anthropic is a team sport&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excitement about AI&#39;s potential to transform how enterprises operate, and a genuine desire to help customers succeed with it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to travel regularly for customer engagements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
