&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced IP Counsel to help protect some of the world&#39;s fastest-growing technology brands. In this role, you will share ownership of Anthropic&#39;s global trademarks and domains practice, spanning clearance, prosecution, portfolio management, and enforcement, partnering closely with other members of our IP team, outside counsel, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s brands are among its most valuable assets, and you will help protect them at the pace the AI industry moves. Our trademark practice spans a rapidly growing global portfolio, a high-volume enforcement program, and naming decisions for some of the most visible products in technology. This is a hands-on role for an attorney with deep trademark expertise who wants their work to matter and who is aligned with Anthropic&#39;s mission of responsible AI development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run trademark clearance for new model, product, and feature names, delivering clear, risk-rated recommendations that let teams move quickly and confidently&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage global trademark prosecution and portfolio strategy in coordination with outside counsel, including filing strategy, office actions, and portfolio maintenance across many jurisdictions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead trademark and domain enforcement end to end: assess potential infringements, select the right enforcement mechanism, work with outside counsel as necessary, and drive matters to resolution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help oversee our online brand protection program, working with our external vendor and IP Legal Specialist to action infringements and impersonations at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage domain portfolio strategy, including acquisitions, disputes, and recovery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Respond to inbound trademark demands and support trademark-related litigation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Counsel marketing, product, and go-to-market teams on brand usage and naming, translating IP risk into practical guidance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the playbooks and processes that let a lean team run a world-class global brand protection practice&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold a law degree (JD, LLB, or equivalent) and meet the local licensing requirements to work as in-house counsel where you&#39;ll be based&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have substantial trademark and domain practice experience spanning clearance, prosecution, portfolio management, and enforcement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have current, hands-on experience: running clearances, shape filing strategies, and make enforcement calls yourself&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have managed global trademark and domain portfolios, including UDRP proceedings and online enforcement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exercise sound judgment about which matters to pursue, and can explain that reasoning clearly to lawyers and non-lawyers alike&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work collaboratively with legal colleagues, outside counsel, and business partners, and are motivated by the work itself&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of trademark and domain practice&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior in-house experience at a technology company, with a track record of partnering with business teams to enable speed in a risk-adjusted way&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience protecting brands in AI or other rapidly evolving technology fields&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building or scaling high-volume enforcement and takedown programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience navigating brand disputes with commercial, community, or publicity dimensions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
