&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager, Compute Accounting at Anthropic, you will execute day-to-day accounting for our compute and cloud infrastructure spend, ensuring accurate financial reporting and robust controls as we scale. You&#39;ll be responsible for preparing compute cost accounting, including accruals, prepaids, accounts payable reconciliation, expense classification, and commitment tracking. This role requires hands-on month-end close experience, strong organizational skills, and the ability to build scalable processes and controls in a high-growth environment, with a strong appetite for process improvement and automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work directly with Engineering, Procurement, and Finance &amp;amp; Strategy to resolve issues and ensure that costs are captured accurately and in compliance with our agreements. As Anthropic&#39;s compute footprint expands rapidly across multiple cloud service providers, you&#39;ll help operate the financial controls and processes that enable us to manage compute spend measured in the tens of billions of dollars with precision and confidence. You&#39;ll also support internal and external audit requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accounting lifecycle for compute and cloud infrastructure expenses, ensuring accurate and timely recording of all costs through monthly close, reconciliations, accruals, prepaids, journal entries, and flux analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and interpret cloud service provider and infrastructure contracts to ensure proper accounting treatment, commitment tracking, and compliance with contractual terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and reconcile commitment-based agreements, ensuring proper recognition and disclosure of multi-year purchase obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform accounts payable and vendor statement reconciliations, working with cloud service providers to resolve discrepancies and ensure billing accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable processes and controls that can grow with the organization, and develop reporting and monitoring systems to provide visibility into compute spending patterns and trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audit requests on compute cost accounting and commitment disclosure matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering and cloud service providers to investigate issues and see them through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build monthly and quarterly financial reporting packages for leadership reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvement and automation initiatives—redesigning close workflows, building automated data pipelines and reporting, and leveraging AI tooling—and contribute to cross-functional projects from scoping through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive operational accounting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA (or equivalent) with a strong understanding of GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, hands-on month-end close experience, with a proven ability to prepare accruals, reconciliations, and journal entries accurately and on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience accounting for cloud service or compute infrastructure expenses, including review of associated contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud service provider cost structures and the unique challenges of accounting for consumption-based services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain issues to vendors, engineers, and other non-finance stakeholders in clear, simple terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical abilities and comfort working with a high volume of transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building accounting processes, controls, and policy in high-growth environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with a track record of seeing issues through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with modern ERP systems (Workday preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience mentoring junior accounting professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading process transformation, automation, or finance systems projects from scoping through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to dive deep into large datasets to identify issues and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with cross-functional partnership in fast-paced environments where priorities can shift quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL and BigQuery proficiency, enabling direct data analysis and validation against source systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python skills for building automation and analytical tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at cloud service providers, data center operators, or technology companies with consumption-based or usage-based business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background combining Big 4 accounting experience with industry roles at technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to infrastructure lease or asset structures, including colocation, GPU clusters, networking equipment, or data center buildouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of implementing automated reconciliation and reporting solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with commitment-based purchasing agreements and their accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI-assisted tools (including Claude) for enhancing financial analysis, memo drafting, and close automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting rapid growth and scaling initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
