&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is changing what security teams can do. Claude can find and help fix vulnerabilities in code at a pace that wasn&#39;t possible a year ago, and we want defenders to have that advantage first.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Manager, Cybersecurity Sales Specialists, you&#39;ll build and lead the team of cybersecurity specialists who sell to security teams across our Americas business units, including financial services, healthcare and life sciences, and technology. Your team partners with the Account Executives in each industry to lead the security strategy and the security deal with CISOs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll help shape how Anthropic sells security: how your team covers the business units, how it works with the Account Executive and Applied AI organizations, and how what we learn from customers shapes what we build. The work matters to our mission: a safe transition through transformative AI depends on the people who defend critical systems being able to use it well, and this team is how we get it into their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hire, onboard and develop a high-performing team of cybersecurity sales specialists&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own your team&#39;s forecast, pipeline health and results across the business units you cover&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set your team&#39;s coverage model, and agree on clear rules of engagement with the sales leaders who own each industry and with Applied AI leadership on discovery, proofs of concept and architecture&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build a pipeline engine with the Account Executives, across their existing accounts and through outbound to security leaders, events and partners&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coach your team through complex deals that lead with the customer&#39;s problem (finding and fixing vulnerabilities, application security, security operations, and deploying AI agents securely), and act as executive sponsor with CISOs on the most important ones&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make security reviews, verification for security use cases, and procurement a repeatable path rather than a deal-by-deal effort&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scale enablement so Account Executives across every business unit can spot and qualify security opportunities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring what your team hears from security customers to sales leadership and to our product, safeguards and marketing teams, and turn it into input on the roadmap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run a healthy team: clear expectations, regular feedback, and performance and development conversations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building and leading a cybersecurity sales team that carried a number, whether direct, specialist or overlay, including hiring, coaching and managing performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record of closing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise deals where the security organization was the buyer or the deciding approver, and of coaching others to do the same&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fluency in how security teams work, built by selling directly to CISOs, application security leads and security engineers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depth in at least one security domain, such as application security, vulnerability management, security operations, cloud, data, identity or endpoint security&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;History of building a business before there was an established approach, through outbound and partners rather than inherited accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to lead through influence as well as authority, so that Account Executives and their leaders bring your team in because it helps them win&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consultative approach to selling and coaching: understanding the problem before proposing anything, and being honest about what a product can&#39;t do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commitment to making AI systems safe and beneficial&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background selling security in one of the industries we cover, and an understanding of how security is bought and regulated there&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing managers and individual contributors, or scaling a sales team through fast growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading teams selling AI, developer or data platform products to technical buyers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent as a security practitioner or sales engineer before moving into sales leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$450,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$550,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;164e6f48-89e9-4425-ac68-79efd3df81fd&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of our Enterprise Asset &amp;amp; Wealth Management sales organization, you will build and lead a team that brings transformational AI to the world&#39;s leading asset managers, wealth managers, and private markets firms. These are organizations rethinking how they generate investment insight, serve clients and advisors, scale personalization, and meet fiduciary and regulatory obligations. They are looking for a partner they trust to take frontier AI from promising pilots into production at the core of their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a broad portfolio of major AWM institutions at very different stages of AI adoption, from firms already running Claude in production to those just beginning their journey. Your coverage will span global and regional asset managers, alternatives managers, and wealth businesses. You will lead Account Executives, design the coverage and territory model, and build the repeatable, AWM-specific plays that turn early wins into durable, scaled adoption across research, portfolio and client operations, advisor productivity, and compliance and supervision. The selling is technical and multi-stakeholder: platform decisions, model governance, security and procurement rigor, and solutions built on Claude through our API, Claude for Enterprise, Claude Code, and partner cloud platforms. You will shape strategy and operating rhythm while staying personally engaged with executives on the pursuits that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to build an organization, not just run a number: to shape how the asset and wealth management industry adopts frontier AI, and to do it at a company where safety, trust, and long-term customer outcomes are central to how we sell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;key-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define AWM go-to-market strategy and coverage design, including segmentation across asset managers, alternatives managers, and wealth platforms, territories, account prioritization, and vertical value propositions, and evolve the coverage model as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, and retain Enterprise Account Executives with deep asset and wealth management and platform-selling expertise; develop leadership talent and create career paths that keep top performers growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Codify the use cases, proof points, reference stories, and sales motions that make wins repeatable across AWM, such as investment research and idea generation, portfolio and client reporting, RFP and due diligence automation, advisor productivity and client personalization, and compliance and supervision workflows, partnering with Marketing, Enablement, and partner teams to scale them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage personally with C-level and business-line executives (CEOs, CIOs, COOs, Chief Data and AI Officers, Heads of Distribution, and Heads of Wealth) on priority pursuits, building business cases and value narratives and navigating complex procurement, security, model-risk, and legal processes through to production deployment and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the organization&#39;s revenue targets and operating rhythm, instilling pipeline-generation discipline and running forecasting, deal inspection, and account planning cadences that make performance predictable and coachable across a high-volume book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Applied AI, Solutions Architecture, and Product to design solutions, prove value quickly, and translate AWM needs, including fiduciary, books-and-records, and client-data requirements, into product and roadmap input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate cross-functional and partner motions with Customer Success, Marketing, Partnerships, Legal, cloud partners, and the data and technology providers that AWM firms rely on, to deliver a seamless customer experience, and represent Anthropic with customers and at industry events as a visible, trusted leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;minimum-qualifications&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading enterprise sales teams that sell technical, complex products such as API-first platforms, cloud infrastructure, or data and machine learning platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of winning and growing enterprise customers, including building C-suite relationships, in asset and wealth management (asset managers, alternatives managers, private banks, wealth platforms, or the technology and data providers that serve them)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing go-to-market coverage for an enterprise sales team, including segmentation, territories, and account prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational rigor across both a high-volume pipeline and complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles, balancing velocity with deal quality and forecasting accurately in fast-changing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credibility with technical buyers and builders, and with investment and distribution leaders: CIOs, CTOs, CDOs, Heads of AI/ML, Heads of Research, and Heads of Wealth or Distribution, plus experience pairing effectively with solutions architects and applied AI teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coaching skills that raise team performance through deal coaching and account strategy, combined with personal effectiveness alongside executives on high-priority opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in deploying AI responsibly and motivation to advance Anthropic&#39;s mission of building safe, beneficial AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading other sales leaders (second-line management), or demonstrated readiness to step into that scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or meaningfully scaling a verticalized or multi-segment sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience bringing generative AI or LLM-based products, or other emerging platform technologies, to large asset managers, wealth managers, or private markets firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AWM use cases and buyers, such as investment research and portfolio analytics, client reporting and RFP automation, advisor and relationship-manager productivity, and fund operations and servicing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with regulated-industry selling in AWM, including fiduciary and suitability obligations, SEC and FINRA expectations on supervision and books and records, model-risk management, client-data privacy, security review, and the governance expectations of financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling with and through cloud and ecosystem partners such as AWS, Google Cloud, and global systems integrators, as well as the data, analytics, and portfolio-technology vendors embedded in AWM firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with consumption- or usage-based commercial models and value-based pricing conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading organizations through rapid growth, re-segmentation, or significant change&lt;/li&gt;
