&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Claude Partner Network is how consulting firms, systems integrators, and other services partners build practices around Claude. When a company chooses a partner, it wants to know which firms have done this work well, in its industry and for its use case. Specializations are how the program will give it: credentials showing that a partner has demonstrated expertise in a given domain area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Partner Specializations Lead, you&#39;ll own this program end to end: the requirements a firm has to meet, the evidence review that decides who qualifies, the benefits that make a specialization worth earning, and the operating rhythm that keeps it credible year after year. Your job is to take an early framework into a structure that scales: opening it to thousands of partners, running evaluation cycles, and launching new specializations with cross-functional input.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone who likes owning a standard. You&#39;ll work with partner managers, operations, enablement, marketing, and industry teams who each hold a piece of the program, and with senior leaders at partner firms who care a great deal about the outcome. A specialization only means something if it&#39;s earned, so you&#39;ll need to be rigorous with evidence, consistent in your decisions, and firm and clear when the answer is no.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own each specialization&#39;s requirements, evidence standards, and benefits, and keep them current as our products and the partner network change&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run each evaluation cycle from invitation to decision: collect partner evidence, reconcile it against internal data, lead the review, and document every decision&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make and defend qualification decisions, including borderline cases, and apply the standard consistently across firms of very different sizes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate outcomes to partner executives and their Anthropic account teams, including clear guidance for firms that did not qualify&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open the program to the wider partner network, and recommend which specializations come next based on customer demand, partner readiness, and Anthropic&#39;s priorities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define the evidence standard for new specializations with Applied AI, Product, and industry go-to-market teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coordinate the teams that deliver the program&#39;s benefits (marketing, the partner directory, field enablement, technical support) so that earning a specialization leads to something real&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with Partner Enablement so that partner learning paths and certifications support each specialization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the operating rhythm: renewal, remediation periods, an appeals path, and the tracking and reporting that show whether the program is working&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design the review process to scale, using Claude and automation so that routine steps don&#39;t depend on a person&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write and maintain partner-facing guidance (program guide sections, FAQs, application materials), clear enough for a partner to know where it stands without asking us, and internal guidance for field teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use program data to recommend where each requirement&#39;s bar should sit and when it should move, and bring those recommendations to partner leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience owning an external-facing program with published requirements (a partner, channel, certification, accreditation, or similar program), including running at least one full evaluation, qualification, or renewal cycle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience making qualification or eligibility decisions against a written standard and communicating those decisions, including declines, to senior external stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with CRM or PRM data, such as Salesforce reports or a partner portal, as a regular part of your job&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong writing: able to produce clear program requirements, decision memos, and partner-facing guidance that need little editing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading work to a fixed date across several teams you do not manage, such as operations, marketing, enablement, and field teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work effectively where the process is still being built and the details are still changing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are excited about Anthropic&#39;s mission to develop AI that is safe and beneficial&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
