&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s People Legal team is looking for a Lead Employment Counsel to build the legal foundation for our growing workforce across Asia-Pacific. You&#39;ll partner closely with our People team and business leaders to design and run employment programs in the region that help our people do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role pairs deep employment law expertise with pragmatism and creativity. You&#39;ll build structures that manage legal risk across several APAC countries today and that will hold up as our presence in the region scales. You&#39;ll also help colleagues around the world understand how local requirements shape the way we hire, manage, and support people in APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the primary employment lawyer for Anthropic&#39;s APAC region, partnering with People and business leaders across People programs, policies and day-to-day issues&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain the legal infrastructure for new and existing APAC jurisdictions, including Japan, South Korea, Australia, Singapore and India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advise on market entry and workforce structuring, including acquisitions, employer of record arrangements, contractor classification, and headcount thresholds that trigger local obligations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Compensation, Benefits, and Equity teams so that global programs are compliant and scalable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guide employee relations matters, including workplace investigations, in line with local law and practice&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and manage strategy on employment disputes across the region, from pre-litigation claims through tribunal and court proceedings, in partnership with outside counsel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track legislative and regulatory developments across the region, including employee data privacy and emerging rules on AI in employment, and turn them into practical guidance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop scalable templates, playbooks, and training that enable stakeholders to operate compliantly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold a law degree (JD, LLB, or equivalent) and meet the local licensing requirements to work as in-house counsel where you&#39;ll be based&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have deep subject-matter expertise on employment law across multiple APAC countries&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write clearly and concisely, and can provide actionable guidance to non-lawyers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Balance legal risk with business practicality, and work collaboratively with legal and business cross-functional partners&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work effectively with colleagues and stakeholders across multiple time zones&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least 12+ years of relevant employment legal experience across law firms and in-house, with demonstrated experience supporting companies through rapid growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience advising People and business teams on the practical application of employment laws in Japan, South Korea, India, Australia, and Singapore&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creative and pragmatic in your approach to developing legal solutions to business problems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of employee data privacy requirements across the region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
