&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is seeking a Privacy Counsel to join our Legal team. You&#39;ll counsel on complex privacy issues and build the processes and programs that address privacy and data protection in a global context. This is a unique opportunity to join a dynamic and growing team, where you will have the chance to shape the company&#39;s privacy and data protection strategy and compliance program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of novel legal questions, fast-moving product development, and a high-profile regulatory environment, partnering cross-functionally with Legal, Integrity &amp;amp; Compliance, Safeguards, Security, Policy, Research and Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counsel product, research and engineering teams across the model and product lifecycles, applying laws written before frontier AI with clarity and fresh thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical architecture into clear, actionable risk advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver integrated guidance on safety, security and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead privacy on Anthropic&#39;s most strategic deals and partnerships, opening creative paths for novel technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate privacy and data protection terms in enterprise, platform and partnership commercial agreements, including DPAs, BAAs, data sharing agreements and cross-border transfer terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead privacy diligence on mergers and acquisitions, and support corporate governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with counsel and privacy colleagues on joint analysis, bringing competing views together into a single, well-reasoned position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold a law degree (JD, LLB, or equivalent) and meet the local licensing requirements to work as in-house counsel where you&#39;ll be based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience advising a technology business (in-house or at a leading law firm) on privacy and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience drafting and negotiating data protection agreements, such as DPAs, BAAs and data sharing agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of key global privacy laws, including those of the Americas, EEA and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and engage with technical documentation, such as system designs and architecture diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent legal writing, including clear, concise advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years of privacy and data protection legal experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with software and model development and architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build privacy processes, playbooks and templates that scale with a fast-growing business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct engagement with privacy regulators, including providing briefings and responding to inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privacy and data protection work on mergers, acquisitions, and similar transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background advising safety, security or trust and safety teams, including on privacy incidents and notification decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Role-specific policy: For this role, we expect all staff to be able to work from our San Francisco or New York office at least 3 days a week, though we encourage you to apply even if you might need some flexibility for an interim period of time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
