&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Product Counsel, you will be a hands-on legal partner to the teams building Claude for consumers and businesses. You&#39;ll work across Claude&#39;s apps, subscriptions, growth programs and enterprise offerings, moving to wherever the need is greatest. You&#39;ll learn from experienced product lawyers, get close to the product quickly, and take on more ownership as you go. This is a generalist role for someone who wants range, likes a fast pace, and is ready to do the routine work and the novel work with the same care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Design and other cross-functional teams to give clear, practical legal guidance from early ideas through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review product launches across Claude&#39;s consumer and enterprise offerings, spotting issues early and helping teams find a path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on subscriptions, pricing, promotions, billing and other growth programs, including consumer protection and marketing rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support enterprise and regulated-industry products on topics such as admin controls, customer commitments and enterprise readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and review user-facing terms, disclosures, in-product copy and marketing claims&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull in privacy, commercial, IP, safety and other specialists, then return one integrated answer to your product partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build guides, templates and AI-powered workflows so routine questions get answered quickly and the team can focus on novel ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick up new areas as priorities shift, and help with incidents and escalations when they come up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold a law degree (JD, LLB, or equivalent) and meet the local licensing requirements to work as in-house counsel where you&#39;ll be based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4 years of relevant legal experience, with exposure to technology, consumer or regulated products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising business or product teams directly, not only other lawyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of at least two of: consumer protection, privacy, advertising and marketing law, technology transactions, IP, or regulated industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about how AI products work, and the ability to pick up technical concepts quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of making a clear recommendation, even with incomplete information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort moving between assignments as priorities change, with no job too big or too small&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise writing that non-lawyers can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to feedback and a track record of improving quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools in your legal work, or a strong interest in learning to do so&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy and a service orientation, with a real commitment to Anthropic&#39;s mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house product counsel experience, or a secondment with a product team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with subscription businesses, promotions, or consumer billing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise SaaS or regulated customers such as healthcare or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building playbooks, self-serve guidance or legal automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
