&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Claude Platform (API) is how developers and enterprises build with Claude, directly and through our cloud partners. It runs on a consumption model, and the economics move quickly as new models and capabilities launch, serving costs change, and customer usage scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Finance &amp;amp; Strategy Lead to own planning and forecasting for the Claude Platform, run the business reviews that track its performance, and recommend how the products and business should evolve. You&#39;ll sit on the Product Finance &amp;amp; Strategy team and partner with leaders from product, engineering, go-to-market, and other finance teams to steer the growth of the business. This is a finance role close to the product: your forecasts and analyses will shape where the business invests and how it grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead financial planning and analysis for the Claude Platform (API) business across self-serve, enterprise, and cloud partner channels. Set targets for the business and drive interlock with go-to-market partners on targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run the rhythm of business for the Claude Platform with product and cross-functional leaders, including monthly executive reviews with clear analyses and actionable insights to grow the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain financial models and scenario analyses that show how launches, pricing changes, and commitment structures affect the forecast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases for new platform features and products, working with product, engineering, and go-to-market partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to product and finance leaders, analyzing usage, revenue, and cost data to flag what matters and answer complex questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate recurring reporting and lead analyses on whether pricing and new business models are working and what to change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with operations, data science, deal desk, and accounting to ensure new products are billed, reported, and forecasted accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading annual planning and forecasting for a business or product line, from assumptions through final targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building driver-based forecasts for consumption-based or usage-based businesses, including reconciling top-down targets with bottom-up views&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running recurring business reviews with executives, including explaining variances to plan and recommending actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling skills in spreadsheets, and comfort pulling and analyzing your own data in SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping pricing, business model, or investment decisions with analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to partner with product and cross-functional teams and explain financial tradeoffs clearly, in writing and in conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment with incomplete data, and comfort making a call and revisiting conclusions as you learn more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in AI and a commitment to Anthropic&#39;s mission of building safe, beneficial AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategic finance, product finance, FP&amp;amp;A, investment banking, consulting, or a closely related analytical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure, cloud, or developer platform businesses, and a basic understanding of how compute costs and capacity drive unit economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to pricing APIs, developer tools, or cloud services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with how large language models are served, including token-based pricing and inference cost drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in AI, ML, or related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
