&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Manager, Enterprise Industries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager at Anthropic, you&#39;ll lead a team of Enterprise Account Executives driving the adoption of safe, frontier AI by securing strategic deals with leading enterprises. You&#39;ll leverage your leadership and consultative sales expertise in the Industries sector to propel revenue growth while developing a high-performing team of AEs. Working closely with Applied AI Engineering and Product teams, you&#39;ll help Industries customers embed and deploy AI while uncovering its full range of capabilities across their business. In collaboration with GTM and Marketing teams, you&#39;ll continuously refine our value proposition, sales methodology, and market positioning to resonate with enterprise decision-makers and ensure differentiated value across the Industries landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have a passion for developing people, identifying market opportunities within Industries, and executing strategies to capture them. By leading the deployment of Anthropic&#39;s emerging products, you will help enterprises obtain new capabilities while also advancing the ethical development of AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing team of Enterprise Account Executives focused on Industries, providing coaching, mentorship, and guidance to drive team success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement sales strategies tailored to Industries procurement cycles and budgeting processes to meet and exceed team revenue quotas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain accurate forecasts, pipeline management, and reporting while ensuring data integrity in CRM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Enablement to develop training programs and resources that accelerate AE ramp time and effectiveness, with specific focus on Industries buying cycles and decision-making processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Applied AI Engineering teams to demonstrate technical capabilities pre-sales and optimize solutions post-sales for industry-specific applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable your team to have credible technical conversations about AI applications in Industries while maintaining appropriate guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships across the organization to drive strategic initiatives within the Industries sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and execute on new market opportunities and use cases for Anthropic&#39;s AI solutions across business units, research and development centers, and corporate functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help your team navigate complex enterprise stakeholder ecosystems including executives, business leaders, IT departments, and procurement offices to build consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and synthesize customer feedback to inform product direction and enhance customer experience for Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously refine the Industries sales methodology by incorporating learnings into playbooks and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of enterprise sales experience in Industries technology, preferably driving adoption of SaaS or emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of sales leadership experience, ideally 3+ leading teams within the Enterprise segment focused on Industries in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and leading high-performing sales teams selling into large enterprises, with demonstrated success in coaching and developing AEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing and scaling sales processes, tools, and methodologies in fast-growing organizations serving Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical acumen and ability to understand complex AI solutions and their applications in Industries, with experience enabling teams to have credible technical conversations with customer stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful partnership with technical teams throughout the customer journey within large enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Industries buying cycles, procurement frameworks, and key pain points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to navigate complex, multithreaded sales cycles across diverse stakeholder groups and drive cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex enterprise sales cycles and helping AEs secure strategic deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational rigor in pipeline management, forecasting, and sales metrics specific to Industries sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to build relationships across all levels, from technical and business teams to senior executives in Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic approach to market analysis combined with tactical excellence in execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for AI technology and commitment to its safe, responsible development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Manager, Enterprise Industries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Sales Manager chez Anthropic, vous dirigerez une équipe d&#39;Enterprise Account Executives qui favorise l&#39;adoption d&#39;une IA de pointe et sûre en concluant des contrats stratégiques avec des entreprises de premier plan. Vous mettrez à profit votre leadership et votre expertise de la vente consultative dans le secteur Industries pour accélérer la croissance du chiffre d&#39;affaires, tout en développant une équipe d&#39;AE très performante. En étroite collaboration avec les équipes Applied AI Engineering et Produit, vous aiderez les clients Industries à intégrer et à déployer l&#39;IA, tout en leur faisant découvrir l&#39;étendue de ses capacités dans l&#39;ensemble de leurs activités. En collaboration avec les équipes GTM et Marketing, vous affinerez en continu notre proposition de valeur, notre méthodologie de vente et notre positionnement, afin qu&#39;ils trouvent un écho auprès des instances décisionnelles des grandes entreprises et apportent une valeur différenciée sur l&#39;ensemble du secteur Industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le profil idéal a à cœur de faire grandir ses équipes, de repérer les opportunités de marché au sein du secteur Industries et de mettre en œuvre les stratégies qui permettent de les saisir. En pilotant le déploiement des produits émergents d&#39;Anthropic, vous aiderez les entreprises à acquérir de nouvelles capacités tout en contribuant au développement éthique de l&#39;IA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constituer et diriger une équipe très performante d&#39;Enterprise Account Executives dédiée au secteur Industries, en lui apportant coaching, mentorat et accompagnement pour assurer sa réussite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Élaborer et mettre en œuvre des stratégies commerciales adaptées aux cycles d&#39;achat et aux processus budgétaires du secteur Industries, afin d&#39;atteindre et de dépasser les objectifs de chiffre d&#39;affaires de l&#39;équipe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Établir et tenir à jour des prévisions fiables, assurer la gestion du pipeline et le reporting, tout en garantissant l&#39;intégrité des données dans les systèmes CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler avec l&#39;équipe Enablement pour concevoir des programmes de formation et des ressources qui accélèrent la montée en compétence et l&#39;efficacité des AE, avec une attention particulière aux cycles d&#39;achat et aux processus de décision du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec les équipes Applied AI Engineering pour démontrer les capacités techniques en avant-vente et optimiser les solutions en après-vente pour les applications propres à chaque secteur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permettre à votre équipe de mener des échanges techniques crédibles sur les applications de l&#39;IA dans le secteur Industries, dans le respect des garde-fous appropriés&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nouer des partenariats solides au sein de l&#39;organisation pour faire avancer les initiatives stratégiques du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifier et concrétiser de nouvelles opportunités de marché et de nouveaux cas d&#39;usage pour les solutions d&#39;IA d&#39;Anthropic au sein des directions métiers, des centres de recherche et développement et des fonctions support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aider votre équipe à naviguer dans des écosystèmes complexes de parties prenantes au sein des grandes entreprises (direction générale, directions métiers, DSI et services achats) afin de construire un consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recueillir et synthétiser les retours des clients pour éclairer l&#39;orientation produit et améliorer l&#39;expérience client du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construire et affiner en continu la méthodologie de vente Industries en intégrant les enseignements dans des playbooks et des bonnes pratiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce poste pourrait vous correspondre si vous avez :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Au moins 15 ans d&#39;expérience en vente aux grands comptes dans les technologies pour le secteur Industries, de préférence dans l&#39;adoption de solutions SaaS ou de technologies émergentes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Au moins 5 ans d&#39;expérience en management commercial, dont idéalement 3 ans ou plus à la tête d&#39;équipes du segment Enterprise dédiées au secteur Industries en France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience confirmée de la constitution et de la direction d&#39;équipes commerciales très performantes vendant aux grandes entreprises, avec des réussites avérées dans le coaching et le développement des AE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience de la mise en place et du déploiement à grande échelle de processus, d&#39;outils et de méthodologies de vente dans des organisations en forte croissance au service du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une solide culture technique et la capacité à comprendre des solutions d&#39;IA complexes et leurs applications dans le secteur Industries, ainsi que l&#39;habitude de préparer vos équipes à mener des échanges techniques crédibles avec les parties prenantes côté client&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience réussie de la collaboration avec les équipes techniques tout au long du parcours client au sein de grandes entreprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une connaissance approfondie des cycles d&#39;achat, des cadres de passation des marchés et des principales problématiques du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une capacité avérée à piloter des cycles de vente complexes impliquant de multiples interlocuteurs et des parties prenantes variées, et à mener des initiatives transverses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience de la gestion de cycles de vente complexes aux grands comptes et de l&#39;accompagnement des AE dans la conclusion de contrats stratégiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une grande rigueur opérationnelle dans la gestion du pipeline, les prévisions et les indicateurs commerciaux propres aux cycles de vente du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;D&#39;excellentes compétences en communication et la capacité à nouer des relations à tous les niveaux, des équipes techniques et métiers jusqu&#39;aux membres de la direction du secteur Industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une approche stratégique de l&#39;analyse de marché, alliée à une exécution tactique irréprochable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un intérêt marqué pour les technologies d&#39;IA et un engagement en faveur de leur développement sûr et responsable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s Integrity &amp;amp; Compliance (I&amp;amp;C) function is building the systems that let us scale responsibly as our products reach more people, more enterprises, and more regulated industries. Our global compliance program is bespoke, reflecting our unique mission and position as one of the leading AI labs operating on the frontier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Regulatory Programs pillar is a key pillar of our overall Integrity &amp;amp; Compliance function and covers a range of compliance domain areas including economic sanctions, US export controls, and regulatory compliance programs stemming from global content and AI regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Sanctions Compliance Lead, you will take day-to-day leadership of Anthropic&#39;s sanctions compliance program and support oversight of our export controls program, supporting the Regulatory Programs lead as a senior leader within the function. This is a leadership seat in a domain where the rules governing AI models and compute are still being written, and where sanctions exposure runs through globally accessible APIs, downstream and embedded-partner channels, and rapid geographic expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the sanctions program end to end: setting strategy and risk appetite with leadership, continuously assessing risk and driving remediation and program enhancements, governing our screening and enforcement controls, directing regulator-facing matters, and reporting on program health to I&amp;amp;C leadership and the Audit Committee. You will partner closely with our in-house Trade Compliance Counsel on interpretation of applicable law, represent the function with senior stakeholders, and lead and develop trade compliance professionals as the team grows. This is a builder&#39;s role at a company that takes integrity seriously and moves fast. You will exercise independent judgment on issues without clear precedent and build durable programs that let Anthropic move quickly while honoring its obligations to regulators, customers, and the public.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead Anthropic&#39;s sanctions compliance program, including strategy, risk appetite, policy frameworks, and the program roadmap, and keep them current as regulations and the business evolve&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent the sanctions and export controls function with senior leadership and cross-functional partners, and step in for the Regulatory Programs lead across the function as needed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuously assess sanctions risk across products, channels, and markets, and own the remediation of identified issues and the delivery of program enhancements, in partnership with Legal, Internal Audit, Finance, and first-line teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct regulator-facing matters, including voluntary self-disclosures, blocking and reject reports, licensing questions, and responses to regulator or third-party inquiries, in partnership with Trade Compliance Counsel and National Security Legal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Govern Anthropic&#39;s restricted-party screening and enforcement controls, including list configuration, thresholds, escalation criteria, vendor management, and exception review, in partnership with Regulatory Operations and Safeguards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the senior escalation point for complex sanctions matters surfaced by Safeguards, Threat Intelligence, Go-to-Market, and Finance, and set the standards by which first-line teams disposition and escalate cases&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advise business and product teams on sanctions and trade controls implications of commercial and geographic expansion, new products and channels, partnerships, and acquisitions, and translate findings into clear control requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support oversight of the export controls program, partnering with the Sanctions &amp;amp; Export Controls Compliance Officer and Trade Compliance Counsel on program priorities, controls, and reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and deliver program reporting on health, key risks, and emerging issues for I&amp;amp;C and Legal leadership, the Audit Committee, and other governance forums&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monitor sanctions regulatory developments and enforcement actions, assess impact on Anthropic, and drive required program changes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop compliance team members, and help shape the structure of the function as it grows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of course, this is just a sample of the kinds of work this role will require! You should assume that your role will encompass other tasks, too, and that your job duties and responsibilities may change from time to time at Anthropic&#39;s discretion, or otherwise applicable with local law&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Substantive, hands-on experience leading an economic sanctions compliance program (OFAC, EU, UK, and other applicable regimes) in a commercial environment, including program design, policy ownership, and risk governance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing voluntary self-disclosures, blocking or reject reports, and other regulator filings end to end, including coordinating counsel, internal stakeholders, and remediation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience assessing sanctions risk on an ongoing basis and owning the remediation of identified issues and delivery of program enhancements through to closure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience governing a restricted-party screening program, including list scope, match thresholds, escalation criteria, and screening vendor management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of reporting on program health and risk to senior leadership, an audit committee, or a board, and of driving decisions on risk appetite with executives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of US export controls (EAR and BIS rules) sufficient to oversee an export controls program and partner effectively with technical subject-matter experts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering with in-house and outside counsel to interpret trade controls requirements and translating them into practical guidance for product, engineering, operations, and commercial teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including drafting policy and preparing materials for senior leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of relevant experience in economic sanctions compliance, including several years leading a program or team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing and developing compliance professionals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience conducting sanctions diligence for acquisitions, vendors, and third parties, including state-ownership and 50 percent rule analysis&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering with trust and safety, enforcement, or threat intelligence teams on account actions and sanctions escalations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exposure to sanctions compliance in software, cloud, fintech, or AI contexts, including globally accessible platforms and downstream access risk&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience in a Big 4 or other compliance consulting or advisory professional services firm, or at OFAC or another trade regulator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in a hyper-scaling tech company or other fast-paced environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sound judgment and the ability to make risk-based decisions and move work forward with imperfect information&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A leadership style characterized by integrity, humility, strategic thinking, and solution-orientation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role-specific policy:&lt;/strong&gt; For this role, we expect staff to be able to work from either our Washington, DC, San Francisco, or New York City office at least 3 days a week, though we encourage you to apply even if you might need some flexibility for an interim period of time.&lt;/p&gt;
