&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and execute a comprehensive marketing strategy for cybersecurity across key segments: enterprise security operations, threat intelligence, detection and response, governance/risk/compliance, MSSPs and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft differentiated positioning and messaging across solutions pages, campaign materials and content for distinct audiences within the vertical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support go-to-market for product and solution launches including sector-specific offerings and relevant MCP integrations and skills (SIEM, SOAR, EDR, threat intelligence platforms, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the alliances team on joint go-to-market with cybersecurity partners, including shared positioning, launch coordination, and integrated campaign moments across security platform and services partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with communications on executive thought leadership regarding AI&#39;s potential to tip the balance toward defenders, including flagship announcements in the context of key security initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the social and content teams on a cybersecurity content calendar that highlights use cases, case studies, and partnership announcements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive thought leadership initiatives and speaking / event opportunities relevant to the security community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable sales teams with compelling materials, outbound campaigns, and pipeline-driving initiatives for security-led enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on which channels and campaigns are driving results and identify opportunities for iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
