&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;b56b3943-e4c5-445a-8537-23fb91ee6b24&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A connected Claude is the difference between a general-purpose chatbot and a real coworker. We&#39;re building the connected enterprise on three fronts: zero-touch activation, a thriving connector ecosystem, and an enterprise control plane that lets organizations adopt with confidence. We own the path from discovering a connector to using it every day: default and suggested connectors, one-click setup, connector requests, and the identity and admin pieces that remove setup friction for a whole organization at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a technical leader who owns activation end to end, from the moment someone sees a connector to their first successful use of it. You&#39;ll also help to shape the foundations that help the connector ecosystem grow, and the governance controls that make it safe at enterprise scale. You&#39;ll partner closely with product, design and data science, and carry real ownership over what we ship next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own connector activation end to end: measure the funnel from discovery to first use to habit, find the biggest drop-offs, and fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run experiments on default connectors, in-product suggestions, connector requests and onboarding flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make setup close to zero-touch, building on open standards like Cross App Access (XAA) and the MCP authorization spec so one approval can turn a connector on for everyone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the connectors people reach for most, like Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace, so the first experience works and keeps working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lay platform foundations for the connector ecosystem: reusable building blocks that make every new connector easier to launch, discover and activate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out the enterprise control plane: admin controls and governance (domain restrictions, labels, permissions) that help security teams say yes faster instead of blocking rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, data science and sales to turn usage data and customer feedback into priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and standards for the team, mentor other engineers, and lead with influence rather than authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;you-may-be-a-good-fit-if-you&quot;&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have shipped growth or activation work: onboarding flows, funnels, experimentation, and measuring what actually moves usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable with authorization and identity (OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SSO), enough to make setup flows simple without cutting corners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built on large platform APIs (Microsoft Graph, Google Workspace or similar) and can debug failures on both sides of the boundary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built platform or ecosystem surfaces that other teams or developers rely on, and care about durable, well-designed APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand what enterprise admins and security teams need from policy, permissions and governance at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and user research to decide what to build, and can explain the tradeoffs to product and design partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-team and cross-company alignment to ship, with influence over authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;strong-candidates-may-also-have&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of software engineering experience, ideally with 2+ years at a Staff or equivalent technical leadership level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributed to or implemented emerging auth standards (IETF OAuth drafts, MCP authorization)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data governance or information protection (sensitivity labels, DLP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built admin consoles or policy engines for multi-tenant SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run growth experiments on activation funnels&lt;/li&gt;
