&lt;ul data-lfile-container=&quot;6de50a80-2898-499b-a2b6-155f551641a1&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate the tools that help product teams ship faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical strategy and roadmap for your area, and make sure its hardest problems get solved, by you or through others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what it means to trust a change, especially changes written by Claude, and build the tooling that holds the bar throughout the software development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build agents that take on repetitive engineering work, such as diagnosing failures, fixing broken tests, and running migrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed with partner teams to find their biggest sources of friction, validate a solution with them, and turn the fix into a product other teams can adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move between building new tools and improving the shared systems that teams already depend on, as priorities shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
